emote-FFI revisit, collab/ remainder, hygiene).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7796:  rpc_ws.cljc + apply wire envelope deleted, lease_composition_test\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7823:  (architect ruling A; remote-FFI-by-composition DEFERRED, revisit\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7832:  apply-envelope deletions, lease_composition migration): the r4/r5\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7860:queue (ShiBi spec round -- capabilities adopted; remote-FFI revisit;\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7864:## 2026-09-28 10:11:50 +0700 — Slice 5 committed (8b5d907b); slice-8 confirm r9 = REQUEST CHANGES (one P1: verbatim envelope), fix r5 dispatched\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7871:  wire envelope / slice-peer test peers deleted, rpc.cljc reworked\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7882:  request envelope is not preserved verbatim -- lift keeps only\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7885:  permits additional keys (\"the envelope remains open\"), so\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7887:  only uses a constructor-made envelope. Verdict REQUEST CHANGES,\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7891:  :yin.k/request-envelope verbatim; lower uses it as :datom and\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7892:  refuses an envelope-less :ffi-request pend as :yin.k/unsatisfied\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7895:  envelope; refusal). Allowed files: ucf/remote.cljc +\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7909:  re-establishable; the request envelope travels VERBATIM\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7910:  (:yin.k/request-envelope; op/args are derived views only; the\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7911:  lower never rebuilds -- apply's open-envelope protocol makes\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7912:  reconstruction lossy); an envelope-less :ffi-request pend refuses\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7921:  (envelope not verbatim) -> fix r5 (GLM subagent,\ndocs/ideas/meerkat.md:26:Meerkat's core principle, stated almost verbatim in the post:\ndocs/jolt-vs-jank.md:181:or a C SHA-256 via `:include`); M2's pure transit codec lift works verbatim\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:816:;; 2. Transaction envelope (application-defined)\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:1056:| **Multi-tuple Atomicity** | Per-tuple only | Per-object only | Via envelopes or multi-attribute tuples |\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:1191:;; Option 2: Transaction envelope (application-defined)\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:399:envelope key, or attachment identity to that source. The reclaim procedure is an\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:404:codebase are the three the design names: an envelope key (`:ws/attachment`,\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:723:| An `:unwrap` seam for envelope-carried lease facts: the one real envelope    | a transport-scoped plan (an API      | review round P4-r2, F2; the sketches model a   |\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md:726:| see it, so `:envelope-key` attribution is unusable against it until a        |                                      |                                                |\ndocs/datomic.md:155:2. Loading the namespace and reading the protocol map — `:sigs` gives **`:arglists` and `:doc` verbatim** (parameter names and docstrings survive compilation in the protocol var's metadata even though `javap` cannot see them), and `:on-interface` / `:method-map` / `:impls` give the rest of its shape. `ns-publics` gives everything else in the namespace. The signature blocks below are quoted, not reconstructed:\ndocs/datomic.md:167:The whole namespace is **four methods, one predicate, and one dynamic var.** Reconstructed exactly from the protocol's `:sigs` — arglists and docstrings verbatim, including the ragged indentation inside `put`'s docstring, which is the original source formatting:\ndocs/datomic.md:271:The full surface, with arglists and docstrings verbatim from `(:sigs datomic.cluster/ClusteredStore)`:\ndocs/datomic.md:307:* **The val write path takes a key and a bare buffer.** `(create-val cs val-key buf)` — no map, no envelope, no revision. The `{:id ... :v ... :ensure ...}` envelope exists only at the raw `KVStore` boundary *below* this, where it is the store's own bookkeeping row. Symmetrically, `get-val` returns `{:buf buf}`, a one-field wrapper with no revision in it. Immutable content-keyed values never touch a rev at any layer.\ndocs/datomic.md:346:This list is a synthesis of what a backend must provide, not a verbatim Datomic spec. Properties 1–4 are **correctness** requirements for ACID transactions; property 5 is a **performance** requirement (the engine still works without it, just slowly).\ndocs/datomic.md:363:The same peer jar ships a later storage SPI for the Cloud-style architecture. It is worth reading against §1 above, because it is the same team's second attempt at the same problem and it discards nearly every complication the original `KVStore` accumulated. Recovered the same way (`:sigs` reflection plus `javap`); arglists and docstrings verbatim.\ndocs/datomic.md:449:Three of those are the substantive ones. **The envelope is gone** — `put` takes `k` and `v` positionally, so v1's asymmetry (a `put` taking one map while `get` takes a key) disappears, and with it the `{:id nil}` exists-false overload. **The revision is gone from the value path**, because content-keyed immutable values have no replace operation for a guard to protect; §1's whole `:ensure`/`:rev` mechanism exists only to make *overwriting* safe, and core2 removes overwriting instead. **Mutation moved from a guard to a function**: `swap!` takes `f` and retries internally, so the read-modify-CAS loop that every v1 caller had to write correctly now lives inside the abstraction.\ndocs/design/dao.agent.mcp.server.md:469:| -32600 | Invalid request           | transport: bad envelope        |\ndocs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md:224:   (not simply passed through verbatim), quote the owner's exact words and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:315:a pack exists only as an optional transport envelope, deferred until\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:380:### D4 — the shape of the medium and batch coordinates [Owner: composition-minted batch token in the envelope, 2026-09-18]\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:406:`:yin/source-medium` in the §8.5 envelope. A retry of one staged, unaccepted\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:517:stored verbatim (D4 fixes its shape later; nil is legal). `lower` and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:546:keys, FFI ops, parked ids, and effect-raising tags/mnemonics, verbatim from\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:592:**U10a — Stream Codec Parameterization & dao.stream.cbor (D7).** Parameterize the single `dao.stream.ws` state machine with an explicit codec profile containing the subprotocol name, frame kind, value-domain predicate, encoder, and decoder. Preserve `dao.stream.transit-json` and its text-wire behavior unchanged. Upgrade the JVM, browser, Node, and Dart adapters to send and receive typed text/binary messages without content sniffing or NUL sentinels. Add deterministic dual-subprotocol negotiation: the attaching composition explicitly selects a profile; an endpoint may serve the same logical-stream identity concurrently through either profile; no silent downgrade is permitted. Preserve the existing envelopes and lifecycle.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:825:  pack allowed only as an optional transport envelope, deferred until\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
