{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '1,85p;140,180p;295,380p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote\n     2\t  \"The UCF facade through `dao.stream.remote` descriptors: lifts a\n     3\t   parked semantic machine's pending wait\n     4\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3) into\n     5\t   UCF data whose cells and stream markers name `dao.stream.remote`\n     6\t   descriptors under the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor profile\n     7\t   (S7.5.3), and lowers that data back into a resumable local wait\n     8\t   through a reflection (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2,\n     9\t   S2.4).\n    10\t\n    11\t   The local side is the engine's own parked machinery, not an\n    12\t   invented shape. A pending entry is what `yin.vm` parks: the\n    13\t   machine registers beside `:stream-id` and `:cursor-ref`\n    14\t   (`yin.vm.semantic` S3.5's park entries, `response-wait-entry`;\n    15\t   `yin.vm.engine`'s wait-set sweep), every handle and cursor\n    16\t   resolved out of the machine's private `:resources` table -- the\n    17\t   lift reads the table, and no entry ever carries a live handle.\n    18\t   The lower mirrors it: fresh resource entries, one per stream\n    19\t   reflection and one per cursor cell (two waiters sharing one cell\n    20\t   share the one entry, S7.5.3), and wait-set entries that merge the\n    21\t   caller's register context verbatim, so a lowered wait parks under\n    22\t   the engine's own sweep exactly as an unmigrated one does.\n    23\t\n    24\t   Where the engine polls a wait at one of its own fixed resource\n    25\t   keys, the lower parks the wait there: a link wait's pair under\n    26\t   `yin.vm.module`'s link-request-resource and\n    27\t   link-response-resource, reflections and entry fields alike, and a\n    28\t   retained request as the engine's own `:request-sent` shape on the\n    29\t   fixed local call-in key -- the receiver's own pair serves the\n    30\t   retried request and the restored response wait reads the\n    31\t   receiver's own call-out, so the fixed keys serve the resumed\n    32\t   program's calls alone. Every response route travels as its cell\n    33\t   and lowers under the cell's own fresh key (S7.5.3) -- distinct\n    34\t   cells stay distinct, shared cells stay shared -- never at a fixed\n    35\t   key, so a migrated route can never misroute a new call.\n    36\t\n    37\t   `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` are plain-data functions,\n    38\t   parameterized by two composition callbacks rather than coupled to\n    39\t   `yin.vm` or `dao.stream.remote` internals:\n    40\t\n    41\t     serve!  : handle -> {:dao.stream/identity id\n    42\t                          :dao.stream/channel chan} | nil\n    43\t               the exporter's own table entry\n    44\t               (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3): nil when the handle\n    45\t               cannot be served -- no table to enter it in, no\n    46\t               channel to the resumer -- which refuses the lift as\n    47\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before minting the value\n    48\t               (S7.4.3).\n    49\t\n    50\t     attach! : remote-descriptor -> {:dao.stream/outcome\n    51\t                                     :dao.stream/ok\n    52\t                                     :dao.stream/handle reflection}\n    53\t               | outcome-map\n    54\t               the receiver's own `:dao.stream/attach` dispatch for\n    55\t               `:dao.stream/remote` (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.4): an\n    56\t               outcome other than `ok` -- including a reflection\n    57\t               already marked gone -- refuses the lower as\n    58\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream identity.\n    59\t\n    60\t   The `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim is checked, not declared: a cell\n    61\t   is published only after its kept cursor survives a round trip\n    62\t   through the channel codec -- encoded, decoded back, equal -- which\n    63\t   is what plain data in the channel's portable domain means\n    64\t   (S7.4.3; `dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3's plain-data basis).\n    65\t   `cursor-codec` is the default codec; a composition whose channel\n    66\t   speaks another passes its own `{:encode f :decode f}` to\n    67\t   `lift-pending` or `lift-frame`. A cursor that does not round trip\n    68\t   -- a host object inside is the case S2.3 names -- refuses the lift\n    69\t   as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value is minted.\n    70\t\n    71\t   Every pending variant of S7.4.3 lifts and lowers: `:next`, `:put`,\n    72\t   `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`, and the linker's `:link-request`,\n    73\t   `:link-response` and `:install` (`yin.vm.linker.md` S7.2-7.3).\n    74\t   `:install` names no stream and passes through unchanged.\n    75\t\n    76\t   Scope: `lift-frame` and `lower-frame` are the frame-level entry\n    77\t   points -- cells are minted and remapped across the WHOLE entry\n    78\t   set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to one UCF\n    79\t   cell and lower back into one shared cursor entry, and independent\n    80\t   cells stay independent (S7.5.3, and the sharing rule of the S7.11\n    81\t   pending-state blocker). `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` lift or\n    82\t   lower one entry into a self-contained table.\"\n    83\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    84\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    85\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n   140\t         (when (= cursor r) cursor))\n   141\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(defn lift-marker\n   145\t  \"The UCF stream marker (S7.5.1) for local handle `h`, its descriptor\n   146\t   the remote descriptor `serve!` mints by entering `h` in the\n   147\t   exporter's table (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2). nil when `serve!`\n   148\t   refuses -- the source cannot be entered, or cannot honor the\n   149\t   profile -- so a caller mints `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value\n   150\t   is produced (S7.4.3).\"\n   151\t  [serve! h]\n   152\t  (when-let [served (serve! h)]\n   153\t    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity served)]\n   154\t      {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream,\n   155\t       :dao.stream/identity id,\n   156\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\n   157\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote,\n   158\t        :dao.stream/identity id,\n   159\t        :dao.stream/channel (:dao.stream/channel served)}})))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn lower-marker\n   163\t  \"The local handle `attach!` gives for UCF stream marker `m` -- a\n   164\t   reflection on the original logical stream -- or nil when the attach\n   165\t   does not answer ok: a reflection marked gone, or any other refusal,\n   166\t   is unsatisfied at the caller.\"\n   167\t  [attach! m]\n   168\t  (let [result (attach! (:dao.stream/descriptor m))]\n   169\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   170\t      (:dao.stream/handle result))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t;; =============================================================================\n   174\t;; The pending wait (S7.4.3)\n   175\t;; =============================================================================\n   176\t;;\n   177\t;; Local pending-entry shapes this namespace lifts, and lowers back to\n   178\t;; -- the engine's own wait-set shapes, plain data resolved through\n   179\t;; the machine's `:resources` table:\n   180\t;;\n   295\t    (unsatisfied)))\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t(defn- lift-write\n   299\t  \"S7.4.3's blocked write: the target stream's marker and the\n   300\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\n   301\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\n   302\t   cursor cell.\"\n   303\t  [serve! resources entry]\n   304\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\n   305\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   306\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\n   307\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\n   308\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\n   309\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn- call-out-cell\n   313\t  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route the\n   314\t   retained call had on the emitter: the cursor entry under\n   315\t   `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, reading the call-out stream under\n   316\t   `vm/call-out-stream-key` at its kept position. nil when the\n   317\t   composition holds no call pair, which no real retained request\n   318\t   does -- the pair is checked before the call parked.\"\n   319\t  [resources]\n   320\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n   321\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n   322\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n   323\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\n   324\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\n   325\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- lift-retained-request\n   329\t  \"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\n   330\t   the request the engine holds unsent. Both endpoints are served --\n   331\t   the request stream's marker and the response stream's marker,\n   332\t   `call-out-cell`'s -- and the retained envelope rides VERBATIM\n   333\t   (`:yin.k/request-envelope`) beside the kept response cell\n   334\t   (`:yin.k/response-cell`), its op and args carried only as\n   335\t   derived views (`:request-op`, `:request-args`; the op is the\n   336\t   source of the lowered entry's `:op`), so a resumer re-establishes\n   337\t   the carried pair exactly as the sender held it: retry through the\n   338\t   request reflection, wait for the response through the response\n   339\t   reflection at the kept position. The envelope is the whole truth:\n   340\t   the request protocol is open to keys beyond op and args\n   341\t   (`dao.stream.apply`'s `request?`), so the lower must never\n   342\t   rebuild it from the views. Either endpoint unservable refuses as\n   343\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that endpoint's identity, before any\n   344\t   value is minted.\"\n   345\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   346\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\n   347\t        envelope (:datom entry)\n   348\t        route (call-out-cell resources)\n   349\t        resp-h (and route (get resources (:stream-id route)))]\n   350\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   351\t      (if-let [resp-marker (and resp-h (lift-marker serve! resp-h))]\n   352\t        (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id route) resp-h (:cursor route))]\n   353\t          {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\n   354\t                     :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   355\t                     :yin.k/request-envelope envelope,\n   356\t                     :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n   357\t                                           (:op entry)),\n   358\t                     :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\n   359\t                     :yin.k/request marker,\n   360\t                     :yin.k/response resp-marker,\n   361\t                     :yin.k/response-cell cid},\n   362\t           :cell? true}\n   363\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   364\t        (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   365\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   366\t\n   367\t\n   368\t(defn- lift-link\n   369\t  \"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair name the engine's own fixed\n   370\t   link keys on a real entry (`module/link-request-resource` and\n   371\t   `module/link-response-resource`), resolved into `:resources`, and\n   372\t   the kept `:cursor` on the response stream\n   373\t   (`module/require-handler` mints it before the envelope is appended)\n   374\t   is the response cell -- a cell like any other, at its kept\n   375\t   position. Both pair markers travel, the engine's `:link-response`\n   376\t   entry retaining its `:request` beside the response side; the\n   377\t   envelope rides verbatim on the request-in-hand variant.\"\n   378\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   379\t  (let [reason (:reason entry)\n   380\t        resp-h (get resources (:response entry))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
